  ('467398619582981003', 'Anna and the Wolves', 1973, 'Drama', 'Carlos Saura, José Luis Ruiz Marcos, Iñaki Akarregui', 'Rafael Azcona, Carlos Saura', 'Geraldine Chaplin, Fernando Fernán Gómez, José María Prada, José Vivó, Rafaela Aparicio, Charo Soriano, Marisa Porcel, Anny Quinas', null, 'The young but traveled Ana arrives in a manor in the countryside of Spain to work as nanny of three girls and finds a dysfunctional family.', 'The young but traveled Ana arrives in a manor in the countryside of Spain to work as nanny of three girls and finds a dysfunctional family.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/faQe1QMwhCDws4OtTEWIjGroSSL.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:107287'),
  ('956573306761230187', 'Anna Boleyn', 1920, 'History, Drama', 'Ernst Lubitsch, Theodor Sparkuhl', 'Norbert Falk, Hanns Kräly', 'Emil Jannings, Henny Porten, Paul Hartmann, Ludwig Hartau, Hedwig Pauly-Winterstein, Hilde Müller, Aud Egede-Nissen, Maria Reisenhofer', null, 'The story of the ill-fated second wife of the English king Henry VIII, whose marriage to the Henry led to momentous political and religious turmoil in England.', 'The story of the ill-fated second wife of the English king Henry VIII, whose marriage to the Henry led to momentous political and religious turmoil in England.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/kuNc1A3g2KMlUzDCpvm2JRhGNNI.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:55644'),
  ('711526247221987924', 'Anna Christie', 1930, 'Drama, Romance', 'Clarence Brown, William H. Daniels', 'Frances Marion', 'Greta Garbo, Charles Bickford, George F. Marion, Marie Dressler, James T. Mack, Lee Phelps, Jack Baxley, William H. O''Brien', 'NR', 'Old sailor Chris Christofferson eagerly awaits the arrival of his grown daughter Anna, whom he sent at five years old to live with relatives in Minnesota. He has not seen her since, but believes her to be a decent and respectably employed young woman. When Anna arrives, however, it is clear that she has lived a hard life in the dregs of society, and that much of spirit has been extinguished. She falls in love with a young sailor rescued at sea by her father, but dreads to reveal to him the truth of her past. Both father and young man are deluded about her background, yet Anna cannot quite bring herself to allow them to remain deluded.', 'Old sailor Chris Christofferson eagerly awaits the arrival of his grown daughter Anna, whom he sent at five years old to live with relatives in Minnesota. He has not seen her since, but believes her to be a decent and respectably employed young woman. When Anna arrives, however, it is clear that she has lived a hard life in the dregs of society, and that much of spirit has been extinguished. She falls in love with a young sailor rescued at sea by her father, but dreads to reveal to him the truth of her past. Both father and young man are deluded about her background, yet Anna cannot quite bring herself to allow them to remain deluded.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/zHsjA95g42xeBEPcWdF4s1BA53L.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:42812'),
  ('200590073132177116', 'Anna Karenina', 1935, 'History, Drama, Romance', 'Clarence Brown, William H. Daniels, Charles Dorian', 'Salka Viertel, Clemence Dane', 'Greta Garbo, Fredric March, Freddie Bartholomew, Maureen O''Sullivan, May Robson, Basil Rathbone, Reginald Owen, Phoebe Foster', 'NR', 'In Imperial Russia, Anna, wife of the officer Karenin, goes to Moscow to visit her brother. On the way, she meets charming cavalry officer Vronsky, to whom she''s immediately attracted. But in St. Petersburg’s high society, a relationship like this could destroy a woman’s reputation.', 'In Imperial Russia, Anna, wife of the officer Karenin, goes to Moscow to visit her brother. On the way, she meets charming cavalry officer Vronsky, to whom she''s immediately attracted. But in St. Petersburg’s high society, a relationship like this could destroy a woman’s reputation.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/39bSsAvMGOgN8I5lt2rOQgAXsj7.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:70881'),
